  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Give multi-pass, chamfer and taper turning the setup stock through additive `multi_pass_in`, `chamfer_in` and `taper_in` APIs; retain the old entry points as no-stock compatibility wrappers.\r\n- Reuse #278's `StockEnv` / `Exit::inside` rule: feed the radial exit at the plunge feed when stock continues beyond the cut, and keep the existing rapid when it does not. Keep axial rapids outside the stock OD.\r\n- Start multi-pass roughing from the stock top and discard stock-empty roughing rungs in restricted windows, preserving the leave floor and every finishing ride.\r\n- Leave the verifier, simulation/posting gates, serialized schema and dependencies unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction and pinning tests\r\n\r\nOn the original production base `b1411ab1`, the three new app regressions fail on the unsafe rapid exits. The existing verifier reports `RapidInStock` and posting refuses each program; this reproduced a caught defect, not silent unsafe output, so P1 is retained.\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/turning_contour_stock.rs` exercises real setup/command generation and posting on a bar extending to Z48 with the cut ending at Z40:\r\n\r\n- `a_multipass_in_a_longer_bar_exits_at_feed_and_posts`\r\n- `a_chamfer_in_a_longer_bar_exits_at_feed_and_posts`\r\n- `a_taper_in_a_longer_bar_exits_at_feed_and_posts`\r\n\r\n`crates/motion/tests/turning_contour_stock.rs` pins all three kinds' same-end/no-stock compatibility, exact path geometry apart from the required exit kind/feed, interior windows and wider-stock axial clearance. `a_wide_stock_ladder_drops_air_rungs_outside_a_restricted_window` also pins roughing engagement and finishing-ride preservation.\r\n\r\nThe app unit control `a_radial_exit_inside_a_longer_bar_is_refused_unless_it_is_a_feed` verifies that the unchanged meridian verifier refuses an intentionally rapid exit at the correct move index.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nExact head: `ced6931dad5c86b7974f8460112f07697b4be961`; integrated base: `be2019759fef54d330d8b37206dc0ef8cf33de33`.\r\n\r\n- Native Windows `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base be2019759fef54d330d8b37206dc0ef8cf33de33`: exit 0; 3/3 steps pass. Final batch: **1,149 passed, 0 failed, 9 ignored** (motion 232, app 866, selected UI 51). This includes both changed library-unit and integration tests; counts are not added to overlapping focused runs.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\r\n- New regression files: `rustfmt --edition 2024 --check`; pinned-base `git diff --check`: pass.\r\n- Independent full static review plus incremental re-review: no remaining actionable findings. Its restricted-window roughing finding is fixed and has an observed red/green regression.\r\n- Clean merge preview against current canonical main `108c84ac`; incoming changes are setup-WCS, STEP import, README and packaging work, with no turning, gate, instruction or dependency overlap. Validation remains pinned to the integrated base above.\r\n\r\nNot exercised: Linux/macOS, full release/heavy lanes, manual application UI or real CNC operations. Hosted workflows are intentionally not triggered by PRs; no hosted CI result is claimed.\r\n\r\n## Readings and decisions\r\n\r\nReuses merged #278's stock/profile exit pattern and the existing contour/profile roughing code. Decision: `docs/decisions/323-safe-turning-exits.md`.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Multi-pass, chamfer and taper turning read stock and feed out of a cut ending inside a longer bar, preserving safe rapid clearance and stock-engaged roughing (#323).\r\n\r\nFixes #323\r\n",
